            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An end effector for use with a surgical instrument, comprising: a first jaw member (250a) defining a longitudinal axis ("B"); a second jaw member (250b), wherein the first jaw member (250a) is movable toward the second jaw member (250b); and a cam pin (224d), wherein: the first jaw member (250a) has a first cam slot (300a) defined therein, wherein the first cam slot (300a) defines a first portion (310a) having a first slope relative to the longitudinal axis and a second portion (320a) having a second slope relative to the longitudinal axis, and the cam pin (224d) is slidingly received in the first cam slot (300a), whereby longitudinal distal movement of the cam pin (224d) along the cam slot causes the first jaw member (250a) to move towards the second jaw member (250b), wherein said longitudinal distal movement of the cam pin (224d) along the first portion (310a) of the first cam slot (300a) causes initial movement of the first jaw member (250a) relative to the second jaw member (250b), and said longitudinal distal movement of the cam pin (224d) along the second portion (320a) of the first cam slot (300a) causes additional movement of the first jaw member (250a) relative to the second jaw member (250b).</p>
            </abstract>
